Z||000002||99BlackZ||02-26-2001||09:58 PM||||That's what I was thinking.  V-8 Fiero and MPG don't seem to mix. . .<BR>If your V-8 is an old carbuerated setup, and is built, theh 15 probably isn't bad.  IF it is a newer EFI unit that is close to stock, then you should be getting closer to 20.<BR>I haven't ever owned a V-8 fiero, but I've owned a few V-8 Mustangs.  My '95 5.0 was built slightly, and even had 3:70 gears, but I still managed 20 - 22 mpg on the highway.  That sucker weighed 3600lbs with me in it too.||||reg||1
